From: DHB_AX local port <local@invalid>
Subject: [LOCAL ONLY] net: stmmac: add a per-instance DMA register base

DMA operations and the descriptor helpers are handed priv->ioaddr, which
assumes the DMA register block sits at the platform resource base.  On
integrations where several MACs share one multi-channel DMA that is not
true: each instance owns one channel at its own offset.

Add priv->dmaaddr, default it to the resource base so nothing changes for
existing platforms, and use it for the DMA and descriptor call sites.
priv->ioaddr keeps addressing the MDIO block.

This also covers enh_desc_get_tx_status(), which reaches
dwmac_dma_flush_tx_fifo() on the TX error path: wrapping the DMA ops in
glue code alone does not fix that call, because it arrives through the
descriptor ops instead.

This is a local hardware-enablement patch and is not for submission.
